0015: rewind mode for test harnesses, off unless bridge.conf sets rewindMode = True in both copies. A test host snapshots the game process and later puts its memory back; the server then returns to the D3D9 state of the snapshot. At the end of a Present the client sends one synchronous Bridge_Rewind command, which leaves both command queues empty, and parks. While a snapshot is held the server defers destroys of the objects alive at it, keeps the old contents of a buffer or surface before the first upload, and on a rewind brings back destroyed objects, lets go of new ones, puts contents, device state and data queue positions back. With the option off no code path changes: the client makes no cooperation block and the server takes no snapshot.
Applies after 0001-0014 on NVIDIAGameWorks/dxvk-remix f35b86a (bridge/ only).
